{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]I was the younger son and I [Gm]wanted it all now
Said, [Eb]Father, give me my share, I'm [F]through behind this plow
He di[Bb]vided up his property, I [Gm]gathered everything
And I [Eb]left for a distant country where the [F]money made me king
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
But the [Bb]money ran like water and the [Gm]famine came to town
I was [Eb]feeding pigs for strangers [F]with my head hung down
I [Bb]longed to eat the pods they ate, but [Gm]no one gave me a crumb
Then I [Eb]came to myself and I [F]thought of where I'd come from
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Eb]I will get up [F]and go to my father
I [Bb]am no longer wor[F/A]thy to be called your [Gm]son
[Eb]Treat me as one [F]of your hired hands
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
While [Bb]I was still a long way [Gm]off
My father saw me on the road
[Eb]He ran to me and held me tight
He [F]kissed me and he brought me [Bb]home
This son of mine was dead [Gm]and is alive a[Eb]gain
He was [F]lost and is [Bb]found
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
My brother heard the music as he came [Gm]in from the field
He [Eb]stood outside in anger and his [F]heart would not yield
So our [Bb]father came outside to him and [Gm]pleaded with him there
My [Eb]child, you're always with me, all I [F]have is yours to share
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]We had to celebrate [F]and rejoice
Be[Bb]cause this brother of yours [F/A]was dead and is a[Gm]live [Gm7/F][Eb]
He was [F]lost and is [Bb]found
{end_of_bridge}

